From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] uiautomationcore: cached element getters, element-valued properties, SetFocus, GetClickablePoint

Most of the IUIAutomationElement getters for cached properties, and several of the current
ones, returned E_NOTIMPL, so a client that asked a cache request for a node's properties
(and patterns' properties) could not read them back, and reading what an element
refers to (labelled by, controller for, flows to) failed.

 - Every Cached getter of the element (including those of IUIAutomationElement5 to 9)
   returns what the cache request fetched, E_INVALIDARG for a property the request did not
   name and E_POINTER without a result pointer; GetCachedPropertyValue is the Ex method with
   the default value.
 - The current and cached element-valued properties (LabeledBy) give the element, or NULL;
   those valued with elements (ControllerFor, DescribedBy, FlowsTo, FlowsFrom, AnnotationObjects)
   give the array, empty when a provider gives none; AnnotationTypes the array of numbers.
 - SetFocus and GetRuntimeId go to the node; GetClickablePoint gives the point the provider says is
   clickable, else the middle of the bounding rectangle, and says FALSE for an empty one.
---
